window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"galio","b":"locke","win":["Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"Ritual Nails reaches 950 to your 825 — you do not win the poke war, so trade."},{"when":"Enemy level 6","text":"His R Purgatory turns your low HP into an execute — the free-trade lane ends here."},{"when":"Enemy first item","text":"Silver Stake scales with your MISSING health — one catch converts, so stay topped up."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Stacked MR blanks his burst again — you win every straight fight from here."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold damage while Soul Ignition burns","HP above his R execute threshold","Grievous Wounds before W ends"],"foe":["Catch you with W down","Bait damage into Soul Ignition","R execute the moment you dip low"]},"early":"Levels 1-5 are simply yours, but not because you out-range him — Ritual Nails throws 950 to Winds of War's 825. You win on damage timing: Soul Ignition (W, 18s at rank 1) refunds a portion of the damage he TAKES while it burns, so everything you pour into an ignited Locke comes partly back. Hold Q and the taunt until it expires, then trade and shove.","mid":"From level 6 through first item the lane goes even — Purgatory (120s) executes you below threshold and Silver Stake's on-hit magic damage grows with the health you are MISSING, so a chipped Galio dies to his autos alone. Stay topped up, keep W for Ashen Pursuit, and spend your own R on other lanes rather than coin-flipping here.","late":"At two-plus items the matchup is Galio's again: stacked MR turns his burst into chip while your taunt and Hero's Entrance decide fights — cast it on an ally within 4000 units, it is not global. Force grouped fights, flank-taunt onto his carries, and never let him find a free pick on your backline — deny the catch and he has no way back.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — W Shield of Durand and your Colossal Smash passive blunt Locke's magic chip before he has any real trade pattern.","Level 2 stays Galio, but not on range — his Ritual Nails throws 950 to your 825, so trade rather than poke.","Level 3 is still yours — with full W uptime you negate the burst windows his combo depends on.","Levels 4-5 remain Galio-favored; before his ult comes online Locke has no clean kill answer while your shield keeps blanking his chip.","Level 6 flattens to even — Purgatory executes a low Galio, and Silver Stake's on-hit grows with the health you are missing.","First item stays even: his Magic Pen spike lets the R threshold convert a caught Galio, so respect his pick range even while you match him in lane.","2+ items swings back to Galio — your MR wall and a 4000-range Hero's Entrance outscale his single-target burst."]});
