window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"galio","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Galio","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-5","text":"Nobody spikes — a chip war where his Q resets an auto into a healing double slash; trade only with shield up."},{"when":"Level 6","text":"Your R does little in the 1v1 here — its real value is roaming, so shove and fly."},{"when":"First item","text":"Shield-tank durability plus Q poke start winning every extended trade — the first real edge of the lane."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Aureate Rush is percent health and his passive revives him; the duel is his."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold E for his Aureate Rush","Even farm through the lane stalemate","First item before he finds a lead"],"foe":["Pull with Dreaded Return","Kill pressure before your item spike","Percent-health damage past your MR"]},"early":"The whole laning phase is a genuine skill matchup — neither of you has kill pressure through level 5, so it becomes a chip war of your 825-range Q against The Darkin Glaive, a 10-second auto reset that heals him. One rule above all: never trade while Shield of Durand is down — Dreaded Return pulls from 850 and his Q recast knocks up, and either cancels the charge.","mid":"At 6 your R is a roam tool that does almost nothing for the 1v1, so shove and spend it cross-map. First item is where the lane breaks your way: shield-tank durability plus repeated Q poke wins every extended trade, as long as Grievous Wounds is answering his Q and Grim Deliverance heals. Hold Justice Punch for Aureate Rush, his only dash.","late":"Two-plus items is his, not yours: Aureate Rush deals percent health, so stacking MR does nothing about it, and Cultivation of War stacks his attack damage and lets him revive once filled. Stop taking the side-lane duel. Group, flank-taunt for your team, buy health and anti-heal rather than raw resistances, and track him on the map constantly.","whys":["Level 1 is even — neither of you has real trading tools yet, so it is last-hitting and light chip on both sides.","Level 2 stays a skill lane: your Q poke matters, but Dreaded Return pulls from 850 and cancels a charging W — trade only with the shield up.","Level 3 remains even; neither champion has genuine kill pressure yet, so it is all wave control and chip math.","Levels 4-5 stay skill-based with both sides trading poke evenly — whoever wins the attrition of your Qs against his sustain takes the stage.","Level 6 is still even: your R is a roam tool that does little against him 1v1, so it changes the map, not this lane.","First item tips it to Galio — shield-tank durability plus Q poke swing every trade, if Grievous Wounds is down.","2+ items is his: Aureate Rush is percent health, so resistances do little, and his passive revives him."]});
